      <p><strong>2 Timothy 4:6-8</strong> — <em>For I am already being poured out like a drink offering, and the time for my departure has come. I have fought the good fight, I have finished the race, I have kept the faith. Now there is in store for me the crown of righteousness, which the Lord, the righteous Judge, will award to me on that day — and not only to me, but also to all who have longed for it.</em></p>
