      <p>The jacarandas do not last. The jacarandas are not meant to last. The jacarandas are a sign. The sign is that the winter is not the last word. The sign is that there is a second bloom. The sign is that the Christian in Johannesburg who has been waiting for a second chance can look up at the purple streets and remember that the God of the Bible is the God of the second chance.</p>
      <p>This post is for the Christian in Johannesburg or Sandton who has been waiting for the second bloom — the Christian who has been asking the Bible for a new beginning, the Christian who has been asking the Bible for a second calling, the Christian who has been asking the Bible for a second spring. The jacarandas are out. The Bible is real. The second bloom is real.</p>
