      <p><strong>2 Corinthians 5:7:22-23</strong> — <em>Therefore, if anyone is in Christ, the new creation has come: The old has gone, the new is here! All this is from God, who reconciled us to himself through Christ.</em></p>
      <p><strong>Revelation 21:5</strong> — <em>He who was seated on the throne said, "I am making everything new!" Then he said, "Write this down, for these words are trustworthy and true."</em></p>
      <p><strong>Romans 8:28</strong> — <em>And we know that in all things God works for the good of those who love him, who have been called according to his purpose.</em></p>
      <p>The Bible treats the second chance as one of the great truths. The Bible treats the second chance as a normal way that the God of the Bible works with the people of God. The Bible treats the Christian who has come to the second chance as a Christian who has been called by the God of the second chance.</p>
      <h2>What the Spring in Joburg Looks Like to the Christian</h2>
      <p>The spring in Joburg in October is the second bloom of the year. The first bloom is the Jacaranda city of the third. The Christian in Joburg sees the second bloom and asks, <em>Is this for me?</em> The Christian in Joburg sees the second bloom and asks, <em>Is the second bloom for me?</em> The Christian in Joburg sees the second bloom and asks, <em>Is the second bloom for me, for my work, for my family, for my marriage, for my country?</em></p>
      <p>The Bible is clear. Yes, the second bloom is for you.</p>
