      <p><strong>Songofun 11:11-12</strong> — <em>See! The winter is past; the rains are over and gone. Flowers appear on the earth; the season of singing has come.</em></p>
      <p>The spring in Joburg is a sign that the second bloom is real. The spring in Joburg is a sign that the Christian in Joburg can look up at the purple streets and remember that the God of the Bible is the God of the second chance.</p>
      <h2>What the Sandton Bible Study Has Started Doing With the Jacarandas</h2>
      <p>In the last three October jacaranda seasons, the Sandton Wednesday evening Bible study has changed shape during the week when the jacarandas are out. We do not cancel the Bible study. We do not change the topic to jacarandas. We do, however, change three things.</p>
      <p>We begin the Bible study that Wednesday with a moment of thanksgiving for the second bloom. The Christian in Sandton in 2026 has had a second bloom. The Christian in Sandton in 2026 has had a second chance at work, at marriage, at ministry, at Bible study. The moment of thanksgiving is real. The thanksgiving is real.</p>
      <p>We read one of the second-chance passages from the Old Testament prophets. We have read Isaiah 43. We have read Hosea 29. We have read Joel 32. The prophets of the second chance are real prophets. The Bible study is real.</p>
