      <p>This post is for the Christian in Sandton who has begun to garden in 2026 — who has begun to plant tomatoes in October, who has begun to think about the watering, who has begun to wonder what the Bible actually says about seeds, about patience, about harvest.</p>
      <h2>What the Bible Actually Says About Planting</h2>
      <p>The Bible is a book about planting. The Bible begins with a garden that was Eden. The Bible ends with the tree of hope. In between, there are many gardens. The Bible treats planting as one of the great pictures of the spiritual life.</p>
      <p><strong>Genesis 1:11-12</strong> — <em>Then God said, "Let the land produce vegetation: seed plants on bare ground, and fruit trees bearing fruit with seeds in them, according to their various kinds." And it was so. The land produced vegetation: plants bearing seed according to their kinds and trees bearing fruit with seeds in them according to their kinds. And God saw that it was good.</em></p>
