      <p><strong>Luke 12:54-56</strong> — <em>He said to the crowd: When it is evening, you say, "It will be fair weather, because the sky is red." And in the morning, "Today it will be stormy, because the sky is red and overcast." You know how to interpret the appearance of the sky, but you cannot interpret the signs of the times.</em></p>
      <p>The gardener who watches the frost will not plant. The gardener who watches the cloud will not reap. The gardener who knows the Joburg spring in 2026 knows that the time to plant is now. The gardener is the Christian who knows that the time to plant in the spiritual life is now.</p>
