      <p>The Christian in Sandton who has begun to garden knows that the patience of the gardener is a small picture of the patience of faith. The Christian who has planted tomatoes in October knows that the harvest is in February. The Christian who has planted the Bible in the morning knows that the harvest is in years. The Christian who has planted the prayer in the evening knows that the harvest is in decades. The patience is real. The harvest is real.</p>
